Template: otzi-headless/restore-from-backup
Type: boolean
Default: false
Description: Restore from a backup?
 If you are reinstalling on a new host and have an otzi-backup file from
 the previous host, you can restore it now. Otherwise, decline and the
 installer will prompt you for fresh configuration.

Template: otzi-headless/backup-path
Type: string
Description: Path to backup file:
 Absolute path to the .otzi-backup file (e.g. /tmp/otzi-backup-...otzi-backup).

Template: otzi-headless/backup-password
Type: password
Description: Backup password:
 The 32-character password printed by `otzi backup` when the file was created.

Template: otzi-headless/role
Type: select
Choices: leader, leaf
Default: leaf
Description: Node role for bootstrap
 During the initial setup phase, one node hosts a bootstrap server
 (the "leader") and the others connect to it (the "leaves") to exchange
 long-term identity public keys. This choice only affects the bootstrap
 step (`otzi setup`). After bootstrap, all nodes are peers in the
 threshold ceremony.

Template: otzi-headless/operators
Type: string
Description: Operator usernames (space-separated)
 List the system usernames that should be able to run `otzi <command>`
 without sudo. Each will be added to the `otzi` group. Leave blank to
 add operators manually later via `sudo usermod -aG otzi <user>` or
 `sudo dpkg-reconfigure otzi-headless`.

Template: otzi-headless/network
Type: select
Choices: mainnet, testnet4, signet
Default: testnet4
Description: Bitcoin network
 The network of the vault. Every node in the ring must use the same one.

Template: otzi-headless/esplora-url
Type: string
Description: Esplora REST API URL (optional)
 Base URL of the Esplora API that the `otzi btc` commands use to read
 balances and UTXOs and to broadcast. It must start with http:// or
 https:// (for example https://mempool.space/testnet4/api); a value without
 that scheme is ignored. Leave blank to use the mempool.space default for
 the network. The daemon itself never contacts it.

Template: otzi-headless/transport
Type: select
Choices: peer-mesh, relay
Default: peer-mesh
Description: Transport kind
 "peer-mesh" — direct WebSocket connections between daemons (recommended
 for permanent federations with stable hostnames). "relay" — daemons
 connect through a central relay server.

Template: otzi-headless/advertised-endpoint
Type: string
Description: This node's reachable address (host[:port])
 Address peers will dial to reach this daemon (e.g. 192.168.1.5:8800).
 Wildcard binds (0.0.0.0, ::) are rejected at parse — use the host's
 routable IP or DNS name. Port defaults to 8800 if omitted. Required
 when transport is "peer-mesh".

Template: otzi-headless/peers
Type: string
Description: Other peers (comma-separated host[:port])
 Reachable addresses of every OTHER node in the ring (e.g.
 "192.168.1.6:8800,node-c.example,[2a11:6c7::11]:1044"). Port defaults
 to 8800 if omitted. The leader does NOT need to be re-typed here on
 leaves — postinst auto-derives the leader-as-peer entry from the
 Bootstrap leader URL.

Template: otzi-headless/relay-url
Type: string
Description: Relay WebSocket URL
 Required when transport is "relay" — e.g. ws://relay.example:9000.

Template: otzi-headless/bootstrap-bind
Type: string
Default: 0.0.0.0:7090
Description: Bootstrap server bind address (host:port) — leader only
 Address this node binds for inbound bootstrap registrations from
 leaves. Used only by `otzi setup` on the leader; ignored on leaves.

Template: otzi-headless/bootstrap-leader-url
Type: string
Description: Bootstrap leader URL — leaf only
 URL of the leader's bootstrap server (e.g. http://leader-host:7090).
 Used only by `otzi setup` on leaves; ignored on the leader.

Template: otzi-headless/node-id
Type: string
Description: Node identifier
 Logical name for this node (defaults to the system hostname). Used as
 [node].id in daemon.toml; must be unique across the ring.
